exports[`--help snapshots > ci 1`] = `
"Usage: testsprite ci [options] [command]

Run tests in CI and scaffold CI integration

Options:
  -h, --help                 display help for command

Commands:
  run [options]              Run project tests, wait for results, and apply the
                             CI gate
  init [options] <platform>  Write a CI workflow that runs your test cases on
                             pull requests (github)
  help [command]             display help for command
"
`;

exports[`--help snapshots > ci init 1`] = `
"Usage: testsprite ci init [options] <platform>

Write a CI workflow (platform: github) that runs the project's TestSprite test
cases against each
pull request's preview deployment; each run spends credits. Replace the
"REPLACE ME" step in the
generated file with your preview URL. Needs the TESTSPRITE_API_KEY repo secret
(see --set-secret).

Options:
  --project <id>       project id to run (auto-detected if you have exactly
                       one)
  --env <name>         environment whose sign-in each PR run uses (default: the
                       project's default environment, written out by name)
  --timeout <s>        max seconds ci run waits for a terminal verdict (1-3600;
                       omitted: ci run's default)
  --path <file>        workflow file to write, under .github/workflows/ (.yml
                       or .yaml) (default: ".github/workflows/testsprite.yml")
  --force              overwrite an existing workflow with different content
                       (keeps a .bak) (default: false)
  --set-secret         set the TESTSPRITE_API_KEY repo secret via gh (if
                       installed + authenticated); OVERWRITES an existing
                       secret of that name (default: false)
  --repo <owner/name>  target repo for --set-secret (gh infers from the cwd if
                       omitted)
  -h, --help           display help for command

Global options (--dry-run, --output, --profile, --endpoint-url, --request-timeout, --verbose, --debug):
  testsprite --help
"
`;

exports[`--help snapshots > ci run 1`] = `
"Usage: testsprite ci run [options]

Run project tests, wait for results, and apply the CI gate

Options:
  --project <id>                  project id (defaults to
                                  TESTSPRITE_PROJECT_ID)
  --all                           run all project tests (already the default)
  --filter <substr>               only run tests whose name contains this
                                  substring
  --env <name>                    the environment whose sign-in the run uses
                                  (unknown names fail). In a pull request, with
                                  --target-url, the run happens in a temporary
                                  clone of it at the preview address, named
                                  github-pr-<N> like a GitHub App run
  --target-url <url>              frontend tests: the address to test,
                                  typically this pull request's preview
                                  deployment
  --skip-preflight                skip the pre-charge reachability probe for
                                  --target-url (default: false)
  --timeout <s>                   max seconds to wait for results (1-3600)
                                  (default: "600")
  --execution-report-timeout <s>  max seconds to wait for the execution report
                                  that fills the job summary (1-3600) (default:
                                  "60")
  --no-execution-report           keep the job summary to the local results
                                  table; read and write no execution report
  --max-concurrency <n>           maximum concurrent polls (1-100) (default:
                                  "50")
  --idempotency-key <key>         idempotency key for the batch dispatch
  --fail-on-skipped               fail if any requested test was not run
                                  (default: warn)
  --allow-empty                   allow zero dispatched tests (default: exit 5)
  --gh-output                     force GitHub annotations and job summary
                                  outside Actions
  --summary-file <path>           write the unified CI summary JSON to this
                                  file
  --report <format>               also write a report (junit); disabled by
                                  default
  --report-file <path>            JUnit report destination (requires --report
                                  junit)
  --report-suite-name <name>      JUnit suite name (default:
                                  testsprite:<projectId>)
  -h, --help                      display help for command

Always waits for results. Failed tests and timeouts fail the gate.
Skipped tests warn unless --fail-on-skipped; missing test ids and unknown
environments always fail. Every selected test is seeded into ONE execution
and the server paces dispatch, as for a GitHub App run.
In GitHub Actions the pull request is read from the event (a deployment_status
event is looked up by commit with GITHUB_TOKEN); draft PRs and deployments
with no pull request are skipped with a notice and zero step outputs. The run
is stamped with the PR, so the Portal links back to it. ci run does not read
the deployment's state or environment: filter deployment_status events with
the job's \`if:\` (state == 'success', not production), or a failed or
production deployment is gated too.
Writes total, passed, failed, skipped, timedOut to GITHUB_OUTPUT when present.
On a supporting backend the job summary is the execution report — the same content
the GitHub App posts as its PR comment — and execution-report-file /
execution-report-markdown-file name its JSON and Markdown for later steps.
Reports and outputs are emitted before the exit code is decided.
Backend tests use the URL in their own code, not --target-url. PR comments are not yet supported.


Global options (--dry-run, --output, --profile, --endpoint-url, --request-timeout, --verbose, --debug):
  testsprite --help
"
`;

